6:1. **Power chip nPM1304** (architecture 17.13 and 17.18; [NPM] pages 24, 28 to 30, 36, 37, 40, 107 to 109, 116 to 120, 146; `design/parts/research-npm1304.md`; `design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md` section 3 K-A7 and section 6 changes 1 to 3). Every nPM1300 name and setting of F4 is replaced. (a) `CHARGE_CURRENT` = 15,000 µA (15 mA, 17.13), termination 4.35 V (register BCHGVTERM value 9, [NPM p36]), termination current 10 % ([NPM p37]); charge time per ring size from 17.17 (section 8.1). (b) The F4 discharge-limit setting is removed: the nPM1304 has none; its battery current limit IBATLIM is fixed, 100 mA minimum ([NPM p28 to p30]); the firmware reads the limiter status bit and acts (section 8.7). (c) Section 8.4 rewritten: ship mode by the ship task TASKENTERSHIPMODE after VBUS removal ([NPM p116]), no timed hibernate; new FACTORY sub-command SHIP_SAMPLE that enters ship mode and keeps the factory flag, for sample rings only (sections 1.2, 9.3). (d) Devicetree properties of the power chip: only those the nPM1304 binding confirms on disk stay plain; every other one is marked TO CONFIRM with who answers (section 8.1).
7:2. **Vibration motor on its own regulator U11** (architecture 17.16 and 17.22; `design/ecad/motor-drive/motor-drive.md` section 2.8 changes F1 to F5): MOTOR enables U11 through R61 and R62 (net MOT_EN); U11 feeds the motor on VMOT from the cell; up to 0.55 ms from MOTOR high to power; no PWM (section 3.1). The fuel gauge does not see the motor's charge, so the firmware adds it (section 8.3). Factory test T-MOTOR reads the battery voltage dip (section 9.3).
9:4. **Battery per ring size** (architecture 17.15 and 17.17): the cell is 18.2 to 24.3 mAh at US 7 up to 24.7 to 32.9 mAh at US 13. Minutes of every threshold use the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh; every hours figure is a range across the sizes; every C-rate is recomputed (sections 1.1, 3.1, 8.1, 8.5, H7).
22:5. **Charging turns on** (review finding F05; 17.5, 17.6, `design/parts/research-charger.md`): the charger is on in every state where the pads carry power (rule R-CHG, section 1.2; action "charge on" in every row into `CHARGING`, section 8.1). The charge current is the named parameter `CHARGE_CURRENT`, still without a value (open item S12); the limit the cell imposes is at most 1 C, 15 to 20 mA; the nPM1300 cannot go below 32 mA, so the charger part is an open hardware choice and the rules hold for whichever is chosen (section 8.1, H8). Leaving ship mode on first power by VBUS stays.
29:3. **Storage 4 GB, about 16 hours** (16.4): CS Semiconductor CSNP32GCR01-BOW, SD NAND in SPI mode, 3.7 GB usable; 16.9 hours on 4,000,000,000 bytes and 15.6 hours on 3.7 GB (section 5.6). The wiring and the driver stack are those of F2.
32:6. **Vibration motor VC0720B088L** at full duty from the 3.0 V rail through Q1 (17.4): same patterns M1, M2, M3, MH, MT, MF; 85 mA maximum (section 3.1; the cell rate is hardware issue H7). **Replaced 2026-11-11 by architecture 17.16: the motor is the Jinlong W0525AB001D, below 80 mA running and below 175 mA at each start; the patterns and the pin are unchanged.**
33:7. **Battery about 15 to 20 mAh** (17.10, which corrects 17.8): thresholds B15, B5, B2 recomputed in minutes (section 1.1); recording hours at 4.0 mA: 3.8 to 5.0, and 1.2 to 1.5 hours at a Plaud's 13 mA (section 8.5). The 10-hour target (requirement P2) is not met (architecture 17.5).
34:8. **Charge current blocked** (17.5, 17.6): the power chip's minimum charge current, 32 mA, is above 1 C for this cell (1.6 to 2.1 C on 15 to 20 mAh). The charging states stay; the charge-current setting and the T-CHARGE limits are BLOCKED on open item S12 and no value is set (section 8.1). The charge voltage is 4.35 V, the cell's type (architecture section 2 and S12).
