583:- **Sudden power loss (cell cut, short, a power-fail reset of the nPM1304 when VSYS falls under VSYSPOF [NPM p107], for example when the load passes the battery current limit, section 8.7):** audio lost = audio still in RAM. Normal case: the chunk being filled plus at most 1 chunk being written = 1,024 ms [CALC]. **Worst case** (the ring full because the card stalls): 3 chunks = **1.536 s** [CALC]. Everything written before is kept: no written sector is ever rewritten during a recording.
591:- S30: free chunks at or under 3,516 = 30 min x 60 s / 0.512 s, rounded up [CALC].
592:- Screen "storage left" = free chunks x 0.512 s, shown in hours and minutes.
593:- The sector count is read at mount. Example for 4,000,000,000 bytes = 7,812,500 sectors: (7,812,500 - 81,920) / 65 = 118,932 chunks (rounded down) = 60,893 s = 16.9 hours of audio [CALC]. Example for the 3.7 GB usable (architecture 16.4) = 7,226,562 sectors: 109,917 chunks = 56,278 s = 15.6 hours [CALC]. Which size the card really shows at mount is not read here (section 10.5).
