657:- Transfer time at full speed [CALC]: stored bytes per recorded hour of 2-channel audio = 3,600 s / 0.512 s = 7,031.25 chunks x 33,280 bytes = 234,000,000 bytes. At the full-speed bulk ceiling of 1.216 MB/s used by the case (19 packets of 64 bytes per 1 ms frame; a USB 2.0 figure the case document marks as not read) this is 234.0 / 1.216 = 192.4 s = **3.21 minutes per recorded hour**; a 10-hour day (not reachable on any cell of US 7 to 13, at most 8.0 hours, section 8.5) would take 32.1 minutes, and a full 4 GB card (16.9 hours) 54.2 minutes. The audio alone, 230.4 MB, takes 3.16 minutes; the 0.05 minutes more are the chunk header sectors (1 in 65). The case document's 6.32 minutes and architecture section 8's 6.3 minutes count the F2 audio of four channels and are out of date (hardware issue H11). The card's read over SPI (at most 2.0 MB/s raw at 16 MHz) is no longer the limit. **[BENCH]** test S2 measures the card read rate; case bench test B1 measures the end-to-end rate.
