768:Between events the application core sleeps in System ON idle (Zephyr idle thread); System OFF is not used, because the GRTC time and Bluetooth must keep running. The motor supply VMOT (U11) is on only while MOTOR is high, in any state; U11 stays on the cell and draws at most 1 µA when off, ship mode included (motor-drive.md section 2.7).
770:### 8.3 Battery measurement
772:- The nPM1304's system monitor measures the battery voltage, the battery current and the thermistor [NPM p99, section 7.1]. The charger sensor driver gives voltage, current and temperature channels (`SENSOR_CHAN_GAUGE_VOLTAGE`, `SENSOR_CHAN_GAUGE_AVG_CURRENT`, `SENSOR_CHAN_GAUGE_TEMP`) [SRC 11; that the family driver serves the nPM1304 is TO CONFIRM, section 10.5 item 3]. Each sample feeds `nrf_fuel_gauge_process()`, which returns the state of charge [SRC 12]; `nrf_fuel_gauge_tte_get()` and `nrf_fuel_gauge_ttf_get()` give time to empty and to full [SRC 12].
773:- **The motor's charge is added.** The chip measures the battery current inside its own path [NPM p99]; the motor draws from the cell through U11, outside that path (section 3.1). The motor player sums the charge of every pulse since the last sample (t_on x 80 mA + 10 ms x 175 mA per pulse, section 3.1; the allowance is an **[ESTIMATE]** until bench step B-M3 measures the start). The current fed to the gauge is I_fed = I_measured + Q_motor / t_sample, counted as a discharge [CALC example: one MF, 51.50 mA.s, in a 1 s sample adds 51.5 mA to that sample]. The sign the library expects for a discharge is TO CONFIRM (section 10.5, item 32). U11 is a linear regulator, so its input current equals the motor current within its own small ground current (motor-drive.md section 2.5).
774:- Sampling: every 1 s in the recording states (thresholds use the mean of the last 10), every 60 s in the other awake states (thresholds use the single sample). Every sample also reads the battery current limit status (section 8.7).
775:- The battery current during a discharge has a full scale of 140 mA [NPM p99]; the chip path stays at or under 55.7 mA with every load on (architecture 17.22).
776:- The fuel gauge needs a battery model of the actual cells; Nordic makes it with its nPM PowerUP application [NPM p99]. One model per ring size or one for all is open (section 10.5, item 4).
786:4. Write TASKENTERSHIPMODE = 1 [NPM p118]. The chip isolates the battery and the main chip loses its supply.
791:Current in ship mode: 370 nA typical for the nPM1304 [NPM p11] plus U11, at most 1 µA (motor-drive.md section 2.7). The cell protection circuit's own drain is not stated (S12).
