816:Caveat, from architecture section 4 and 16.8: the main-chip, storage, radio and power-chip lines are estimates, not datasheet values, and bench test B2 replaces them; the microphone line is from the Knowles datasheet copy at its 2.4 MHz test clock, not at the ring's 1.280 MHz (section 10.5, item 6). The recording figure includes the recording light (1.50 mA at 3.0 V, section 3.2). It excludes the motor (section 3.1) and the screen. **Requirement P2 (10 hours of recording) is NOT met by this ring**: the owner chose thinness over hours on 2026-11-10 (architecture 17.5). In every state other than `RECORDING` the microphones and the light are off.
830:### 8.7 Battery current limit and reset causes of the nPM1304
832:- **The limit is fixed.** The nPM1304 limits the current it draws from the battery: IBATLIM, "Discharging battery current limit", 100 mA in the minimum column, "Validated through simulation" [NPM p29 and its footnote, p30]; the maximum VSYS load from the battery is also 100 mA [NPM p11]. No register sets it. Nordic: "It has not been designed for accurate current limiting", and "If the system load exceeds the discharge current limit, VSYS voltage drops below VSYSPOF causing the device to reset" [NPM p28].
834:- **The status bit and what the firmware does.** Register BCHGILIMSTATUS, field BCHGILIMBATACTIVE, "Discharge current limiter active" [NPM p40]. The specification read names no interrupt for it, so the firmware reads it with every battery sample (section 8.3: every 1 s in `RECORDING`, every 60 s in the other awake states). When it reads ACTIVE:
835:  1. an event log record "battery current limit active" with battery_mv, the state and whether the screen is on;
840:- **Reset causes.** `BOOT` reads the nPM1304 register RSTCAUSE [NPM p146] (bits SHIPMODEEXIT, BOOTMONITORTIMEOUT, WATCHDOGTIMEOUT, LONGPRESSTIMEOUT, THERMALSHUTDOWN, VSYSLOW, SWRESET) and the charger error log CHARGERERRREASON and CHARGERERRSENSOR [NPM p146], writes them into the event log beside the main chip's own reset reason (section 9.4), then clears them with TASKCLRERRLOG [NPM p145]. VSYSLOW means a power-fail reset (VSYS under VSYSPOF): a load above the limit or an empty cell. After a thermal shutdown VSYSLOW can be set instead of THERMALSHUTDOWN [NPM p144].
859:- Update allowed only with the battery above 30 % or VBUS present (always true in the case).
