898:- First charge of step 26 **[PROPOSED by assembly step 26]**: the charger runs at `CHARGE_CURRENT`, 15 mA, to 4.35 V; the jig reads GET_BATTERY until the state of charge reaches 50 percent (500 in `soc_percent_x10`), then goes to step 27. From an empty cell that takes about 0.61 to 1.10 hours across US 7 to 13 [CALC: 0.5 x 18.2 / 15 and 0.5 x 32.9 / 15]. The cell's maker may set another storage level (S12); the reading depends on the battery model (section 10.5, item 4).
904:- Event log (both builds): each state change, fault, battery threshold and transfer command becomes a 512-byte record: magic 0x474C5252 ("RRLG") u32, record seq u32, uptime_ns u64, utc_ms i64, code u16, state u8, reserved u8, 16 bytes of arguments, crash block (below, zero when not a crash), CRC-32 in the last 4 bytes. Records wait in the 4 KB RAM log buffer (8 records) and are written to the log area (LBA 2 to 2,047) at the next time VDD_SD is on; when the buffer is full, the oldest unwritten record is dropped and a "dropped" count is kept.
