998:21. Closed for the chip: in the cool region the nPM1304 halves the charge current, in the warm region it charges to the reduced voltage [NPM p25, Table 12]. Still open: the charge temperature range of the Grepow cell (the cell maker, S12) and the RT1 part, which must have B25/50 = 3,380 K to match the chip's 10 kilo-ohm type [NPM p24] (the schematic owner).
1003:26. The fuel-gauge battery model for the curved cells of 18.2 to 32.9 mAh, the accuracy of its state of charge at 4.1 mA with the motor's charge added, and the cell's discharge limit against the motor start of 175 mA (hardware issue H7). Who answers: the cell maker (S12), then the bench.
1009:31. The cell's highest charge current (open item S12): `CHARGE_CURRENT` 15 mA, 0.82 C of the smallest cell, stays until the cell's maker answers.
1016:Run: `design/.venv/bin/python -I design/firmware-check.py` (exit 0 = pass, 1 = a rule fails). It reads `design/architecture.md`, `design/ecad/ring/netlist.csv` and the Knowles datasheet copy `design/mech/mic-path/datasheets/knowles-spk0641ht4h-1_chipsmall.txt`. Kept from F2 to F4: sections 1 to 10 present; every state of a transition is in the state list, every listed state has a transition out and, except `SHIP` and `BOOT`, one in, and the number of transition rows equals the number stated under the table; every pin and signal name is in architecture section 7, no spare pin is used, and each signal-pin pair matches; the RAM lines sum to the total, at most 512 KB; the charge voltage equals the cell's type in architecture section 2; each PDM clock line divides 32 MHz by a whole prescaler of 4 to 126, uses a ratio of the chip and gives 16,000 or 8,000 Hz; 64-byte bulk packets at full speed (6.1); the motor marking rule (4.7); the schematic rules for the microphone clock (4.5), the storage lines (5.1) and the screen sequence (3.3); thermistor value and ordered limits (8.1); none of the removed names outside the change lists; VDD_MIC on in exactly one state (1.1) and one power-table row (8.2), the recording state; only a long press starts or stops a recording, a short or double press never changes state, and no direction, button or other event touches the recording state; the gesture, centre-source, warning-pulse, hold-off and collision rules of F4; the audio format and chunk arithmetic; one PDM instance; the joystick switches against architecture 17.3 and the 40 ms rule against 16.5; unused pins only on lines that say unused; four pads in order; every row into `CHARGING` and both ship-exit rows say "charge on", `charging-enable` is on whenever VBUS is present, R-CHG stated; section 8.6 states VBUS is an input only; `questions_for_owner` and the RESULT line. Changed in F5 (each replaces an F4 check that asserted what F5 changes): the header says Version F5, follows A5 sections 17.11 to 17.23 and has the list "Changes from F4 to F5" with 8 items; the removed-name rule runs from that list to "How to read this" and now also bans the older power chip's name, the F3 battery range, the old microphone and datasheet names and the discharge-limit property; `CHARGE_CURRENT` is 15,000 µA in `current-microamp`, a multiple of 500 inside 4,000 to 100,000 and at most 1 C of the smallest cell of architecture 17.17, and T-CHARGE has a pass limit (in F4 both were BLOCKED on S12); the microphone mode range is read from the Knowles datasheet copy (F4 used fixed numbers of the older part), the microphone part name is in 4.1 and 8.5, and the gain is 0 dB, the register 0x28 (2 x 0 + 0x28), the header `gain_code` equal to it, and the stored full scale (94 dB SPL minus the sensitivity read from the Knowles copy) equal to the acoustic overload point read from the same copy; section 3.1 names U11, MOT_EN, VMOT and the 0.55 ms delay and never Q1, and architecture 17.22 names U11 (F4 checked Q1 and full duty on VDD_3V0); the battery minutes of 1.1 and the hours of 8.5 are recomputed from the smallest and largest cells of architecture 17.17 and the recording current 4.0 + 2 x (0.63 - 0.58) mA (F4 checked a single range against architecture 17.10); the ship section 8.4 names TASKENTERSHIPMODE, the VBUS removal and EVENTVBUSREMOVED and no timed hibernate; SHIP_SAMPLE keeps the factory flag in 9.3 and in 1.2; section 7 starts with the protocol sentence. New in F5: every "SIGNAL Pn.nn" pair and every chip pin of firmware.md is checked against the U1 rows of `netlist.csv`, and the power chip, microphone and motor nets this file names (GPIO0 on PMIC_INT, LSOUT1 on VDD_MIC, LSOUT2 on VDD_SD, U5 and U6 SELECT, U11 EN, OUT and IN, R61 and R62) against their netlist rows. Rules it cannot check (timing values, protocol layouts, the meaning of text) are checked by review.
